# XSH getgroups()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The supplementary group list is set with pc_drop_groups() (setgroups(),
# not in POSIX, where the system has it) to {65534}; without it the tests
# are UNRESOLVED. getgroups() may also report the effective group ID, in
# any order (implementation-defined); the tests allow both.

assertion  XSH.getgroups.001
anchor     functions/getgroups.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getgroups.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       With supplementary groups {65534}, getgroups({NGROUPS_MAX}+1,
           list) returns n with 1 <= n <= {NGROUPS_MAX}+1, 65534 is among
           list[0..n-1], and every other entry there is the effective group
           ID.
needs      root
test       t/001-list.c

assertion  XSH.getgroups.002
anchor     functions/getgroups.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       getgroups(0, list) returns the count a full call returns and
           leaves list untouched.
needs      root
test       t/002-size-zero.c

assertion  XSH.getgroups.003
anchor     functions/getgroups.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
anchor     functions/getgroups.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       getgroups(-1, list) returns -1 with EINVAL (non-zero and less
           than any count); when the process has two or more groups to
           report, getgroups(count - 1, list) does too.
needs      root
note       With a single group to report only the first case is checked.
test       t/003-einval.c
